# Normalize line endings to LF on checkout everywhere.
#
# The toolchain expects LF: the frontmatter parser, the compliance hook shell
# scripts (which must be LF to run under git-bash on Windows), and the
# validators. Without this, git's autocrlf on Windows rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF, which broke SKILL.md frontmatter detection on windows-latest
# CI. The parser also tolerates CRLF/BOM defensively, but keeping working
# trees LF is the primary guard.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always be LF, regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
